WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.150
Start with what AD actually does,
because most of it is invisible.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:08.887
It trusts the PIV card's issuer
and maps each card to an account.

3
00:00:08.887 --> 00:00:13.874
It hands out Kerberos tickets, so SQL
Server never has to think about tokens.

4
00:00:13.874 --> 00:00:17.825
It autoenrolls certificates for
domain controllers and servers.

5
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:22.075
And through NPS, it answers the
network when a laptop plugs in.

6
00:00:22.075 --> 00:00:24.167
Each of those jobs needs a new owner,

7
00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:27.125
and the right-hand column
shows who takes each one.

8
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:28.687
Some answers are obvious.

9
00:00:28.687 --> 00:00:31.513
Others, like RADIUS, surprise people.

10
00:00:31.513 --> 00:00:33.100
Let's go through them in order.
